     "page": 1,
     "text": "Printed by: ROI_43 11/09/2026 \nCONFIDENTIAL - Contains PHI \nRivera-Brady Clinic | Dr. John Rocha, psychiatry \nPatient: Cassandra Perry DOB: 09/28/1957 Sex: F MRN: 145996 \n\nPROBLEM LIST \n - Bipolar disorder (stable x 7.2 yrs; compliant w/ tx) [controlled] onset 02/2017 \n\nMEDICATIONS \n lamotrigine 200 mg \n\nENCOUNTERS \n\n--- 05/10/2025 Office Visit --- \nS: Cassandra Perry, a 67-year-old female, presented for follow-up of her Bipolar disorder. She reports no recent mood swings or manic episodes. The patient also mentioned occasional mild insomnia but otherwise feels stable. No new complaints. \n\nO: Vitals: BP 137/76, Wt 134 lb. Physical exam: unremarkable. Cardiovascular and respiratory exams are normal. Abdominal exam shows no tenderness or organomegaly. \n\nA: Bipolar is unchanged with current treatment. The patient remains stable with lamotrigine 200 mg daily. \n\nP: Continue current treatment with lamotrigine. Educate the patient on the importance of medication compliance and follow-up. Recommend routine monitoring for any signs of mood changes. RTC in 3-6 months. \n\n--- 11/17/2024 Office Visit --- \nS: Cassandra Perry, a 67-year-old female, presented for her annual physical. She reports feeling generally well, with no recent mood episodes. She complains occasional mild headaches but no other significant issues. \n\nO: Vitals: BP 139/81, Wt 126 lb. Physical exam: unremarkable. Cardiovascular and respiratory exams are normal. Abdominal exam shows no tenderness or organomegaly. Neurological exam is non-focal. \n\nA: Annual physical is improving. Bipolar disorder remains controlled with no recent episodes. \n\nP: Continue current treatment with lamotrigine. Encourage the patient to maintain a healthy lifestyle, including regular exercise and a balanced diet. Schedule a follow-up appointment in 3-6 months. \n\n--- 05/26/2024 Office Visit --- \nS: Cassandra Perry, a 66-year-old female, presented for follow-up of her Bipolar disorder. She reports feeling stable and compliant with her medication regimen. She denies any recent mood swings or manic episodes. \n\nO: Vitals: BP 124/82, Wt 136 lb. Physical exam: unremarkable. Cardiovascular and respiratory exams are normal. Abdominal exam shows no tenderness or organomegaly. \n\nA: Bipolar disorder is stable. The patient remains compliant with her lamotrigine 200 mg daily. \n\nP: Continue current treatment with lamotrigine. Reinforce the importance of medication compliance and regular follow-up visits. Educate the patient on recognizing early signs of mood changes. RTC in 3-6 mont"
