     "page": 2,
     "text": "Page 21  -- ROI --\nhs. \n\n--- 12/03/2023 Office Visit --- \nS: Cassandra Perry, a 66-year-old female, presented for follow-up of her Bipolar disorder. She reports no recent mood swings or manic episodes. She mentioned mild fatigue but no other significant issues. \n\nO: Vitals: BP 131/71, Wt 136 lb. Physical exam: unremarkable. Cardiovascular and respiratory exams are normal. Abdominal exam shows no tenderness or organomegaly. \n\nA: Bipolar disorder remains unchanged. The patient to be compliant with her lamotrigine therapy. \n\nP: Continue current treatment with lamotrigine. Discuss the importance of regular follow-up and monitoring for any mood changes. RTC in 3-6 months. \n\n--- 06/12/2023 Office Visit --- \nS: Cassandra Perry, a 65-year-old female, presented with complaints of a URI. She reports symptoms of nasal congestion, sore throat, and mild cough. No recent mood episodes. \n\nO: Vitals: BP 134/73, Wt 123 lb. Physical exam: unremarkable. Cardiovascular and respiratory exams are normal. No signs of infection in the throat or sinuses. \n\nA: URI is unchanged. Bipolar disorder remains stable. \n\nP: Continue current treatment with lamotrigine. Recommend supportive care for the URI, including rest, hydration, and symptomatic relief. Monitor for any mood changes. RTC in 3-6 months. \n\nSocial: tobacco - cigar current 6/yr \nSocial: alcohol ~10 drinks/week \n\nPage 5 of 5\n"
