     "text": "MURRAY RODRIGUEZ AND PEREZ MEDICAL GROUP - DISCHARGE SUMMARY\n\nPatient: Cassandra Perry DOB: 09/28/1957 Sex: F MRN: 517607\n\nAdmit: 11/24/2023 Discharge: 11/28/2023\n\nPrincipal diagnosis: Pancreatitis (chronic; cause alcohol)\nSecondary: None\n\nReason for admission: Patient presented with exacerbation of chronic pancreatitis.\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nMs. Cassandra Perry, a 66-year-old female with a history of chronic alcohol-induced pancreatitis, was admitted on November 24, 2023, due to worsening abdominal pain and nausea, consistent with a flare-up of her chronic pancreatitis. The patient reported a history of alcohol consumption, approximately 10 drinks per week, and current tobacco use in the form of cigars, about 6 times per year. \n\nPast Medical History:\n1. Chronic pancreatitis (onset 10/24/2009, controlled)\n2. No other significant past medical history.\n\nFamily History:\n- Father: hypertension (onset at age 70), deceased at age 88.\n\nSocial History:\n- Tobacco use: Current cigar smoker, 6 times per year, started on February 19, 2012.\n- Alcohol use: Approximately 10 drinks per week.\n- No illicit drug use.\n\nReview of Systems:\n- Gastrointestinal: Positive for abdominal pain, nausea. Negative for vomiting, diarrhea, constipation, and melena.\n- General: Negative for fever, chills, night sweats, and weight loss.\n- Other systems reviewed were negative.\n\nPhysical Examination on Admission:\n- Vital Signs: Blood pressure 132/70 mmHg, heart rate 78 bpm, respiratory rate 18 breaths per minute, temperature 98.6°F, oxygen saturation 98% on room air.\n- Weight: 130 pounds\n- General: Alert and oriented, no acute distress.\n- HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic. Pupils equal, round, reactive to light. Extraocular movements intact. Oropharynx clear.\n- Neck: Supple, no lymphadenopathy.\n- Chest: Clear to auscultation bilaterally.\n- Heart: Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-distended. Tenderness in the epigastric region. No hepatosplenomegaly.\n- Extremities: No edema, cyanosis, or clubbing.\n- Skin: Warm and dry, no rashes.\n\nHospital Course:\nThe patient was managed conservatively with bowel rest, intravenous hydration, and pain management. Her symptoms improved with treatment, and she was advanced to a clear liquid diet, which she tolerated well. No complications were encountered during her hospital stay.\n\nLaboratory Data:\n- Cholesterol: 274 mg/dL\n- HDL: 34 mg/dL\n- Fructosamine: 227 umol/L\n- Cotinine (qualitative): Negative\n- Gamma-glutamyl transferase (GGT): 47 U/L\n\nDischarge Plan:\nThe patient was discharged home in stable condition"
